message: "If you use this explainer or its cards, please cite it as below. The DOI is that of the gallery (concept DOI, all versions; gallery v1.0.0 = 10.5281/zenodo.23992313)."
title: "Co-reading explainer: the moy-2 reflection-tool line (olm113 → olm127) — an audited figure of what OLMo-3 32B base writes in its proof field when a reflection formula is offered as a tool"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Higashida
    given-names: Manabu
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-7393-2957"
    affiliation: "D3 Center, The University of Osaka, Osaka, Japan"
version: "1.3"
date-released: "2026-11-04"
doi: 10.5281/zenodo.23992312
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/moyhig-ecs/coread-explainer-gallery"
abstract: >-
  An interactive isometric figure (20 states; ja / en; dark / light; also an anywidget for Jupyter / marimo), 1920×1080 stills, a two-voice
  script and a ledger of what can and cannot be said, built from the frozen outputs of a pre-registered line of measurements (the cards
  olm113–olm127 and their frontier controls prf4 / prf5). The cards (PREREG = the frozen promise, RESULT = the read-out) are included in
  cards/ verbatim (Japanese), with an English index. The question text is traced to the public ConstructGap suite (tag v1.0.1) with md5
  at every stage (cards/PROMPT_PROVENANCE.md). Every number on the page is anchored to the data (check_claims.py, 129 anchors).
keywords:
